    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d564">

                <pb facs="0836" n="816" sameAs="frus:frus1950v07/pg816"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795.00/9–2850: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Korea</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Muccio</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Pusak</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-09-28">September 28, 1950.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 28—3 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>215. ReDeptel 151, September 27 [<hi rendition="#italic">26</hi>]. Have continued
                    discourage ROK spokesman’s statements re
                    resolution 38th parallel problem. Have seen Rhee’s speech prepared for his
                    delivery upon entry Seoul; it contains no reference this subject. This morning I
                    called on President, persuaded him not issue any statements re reported peace
                    feelers despite strong insistence foreign correspondents that he do so, and
                    Rhee’s strong personal feeling must ask unconditional surrender.</p>
                <p>Repeated info Tokyo unnumbered.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Muccio</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
